0 R/Alt(Two-column table where one column is titled categories,Ž and the other is titled manifestations,Ž which show cases the individual level consequences of burnout. Some of the categories and manifestations in the table include somatized symptoms such as he\adaches, neck pain, and body pain; mental health symptoms such as anxiety, depression, and mood disturbances; and poorer cognitive function, like poorer prospective memory and delayed memory. ␀)/K 1/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/Figure>>endobj3635 0 obj<</C[/CM26/CM54]/ID(G_SuDYay0UKT0ndDfxqsgg)/K[3671 0 R 3672 0 R]/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/Note>>endobj3636 0 obj<</K 4/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/P>>endobj3637 0 obj<</C/CM27/K 5/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/P>>endobj3638 0 obj<</C[/CM16/CM66]/K 6/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/Caption>>endobj3639 0 obj<</A 3670 0 R/Alt(Two-column table showing the occupational consequences of burnout. The first column is titled categories,Ž and the second column is titled manifestations.Ž Some of the categories and manifestations in the table include talent loss, which leads to the in\tention to leave training programs or a profession; poorer work performance, which manifests itself as absenteeism, reduced ability to work, and less professionalism; and less talent growth, which manifests as reduced engagement in professional developmen\t activities. ␀)/K 7/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/Figure>>endobj3640 0 obj<</C/CM12/K 8/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/P>>endobj3641 0 obj<</C[/CM27/CM65]/K 9/P 3624 0 R/Pg 90 0 R/S/P>>endobj3642 0 obj<</C/CM13/K 1/P 3624 0 R/Pg 94 0 R/S/P>>endobj3643 0 obj<</C/CM13/K 2/P 3624 0 R/Pg 94 0 R/S/P>>endobj3644 0 obj<</C/CM13/K 3/P 3624 0 R/Pg 94 0 R/S/P>>endobj3645 0 obj<</A 3668 0 R/Alt(This figure shows a series of 4 bar graphs, each depicting the levels of burnout versus stressŽ among groups of racial and ethnic groups of U.S. health care workers. Black healthcare workers represented 5.7 percent of the sample, and of this group 42 per\cent indicated they experienced burnout, while 29 percent expressed stress. The next bar graph series are Hispanics, which represented 6.1 percent of the sample group. 45 percent of this group indicated burnout; 33 percent expressed having stress. The thi\rd bar graph series is White \(which was 67.9 percent of the sample group\), and 49 percent of respondents indicated experiencing burnout, while 27 percent expressed having stress. The fourth and final group is labelled preferred not to identify,Ž and re\presented 12.9 percent of the sample group. Of this group, 62 percent indicated having burnout, with 42 percent experiencing stress.   ␀)/K 25/P 3624 0 R/Pg 96 0 R/S/Figure>>endobj3646 0 obj<</C[/CM2/CM54]/K 20/P 3624 0 R/Pg 96 0 R/S/Caption>>endobj3647 0 obj<</C/CM13/K 4/P 3624 0 R/Pg 94 0 R/S/P>>endobj3648 0 obj<</C[/CM16/CM55]/K 21/P 3624 0 R/Pg 96 0 R/S/H3/T()>>endobj3649 0 obj<</C/CM27/K 22/P 3624 0 R/Pg 96 0 R/S/P>>endobj3650 0 obj<</C/CM27/K 23/P 3624 0 R/Pg 96 0 R/S/P>>endobj3651 0 obj<</C/CM27/K[26<</MCID 0/Pg 108 0 R/Type/MCR>>]/P 3624 0 R/Pg 96 0 R/S/P>>endobj3652 0 obj<</C/CM13/K 1/P 3624 0 R/Pg 108 0 R/S/P>>endobj3653 0 obj<</C/CM13/K 2/P 3624 0 R/Pg 108 0 R/S/P>>endobj3654 0 obj<</C[/CM13/CM54]/K[3 3666 0 R 4]/P 3624 0 R/Pg 108 0 R/S/P>>endobj3655 0 obj<</ID(RE3XWEzdekuH2ngqTpG63w)/K[3663 0 R 3664 0 R]/P 3624 0 R/S/Note>>endobj3656 0 obj<</C[/CM6/CM55]/K 9/P 3624 0 R/Pg 108 0 R/S/H3/T()>>endobj3657 0 obj<</C[/CM13/CM54]/K[10<</MCID 0/Pg 111 0 R/Type/MCR>>]/P 3624 0 R/Pg 108 0 R/S/P>>endobj3658 0 obj<</C/CM13/K 1/P 3624 0 R/Pg 111 0 R/S/P>>endobj3659 0 obj<</C[/CM13/CM59]/K[2 3661 0 R 3<</MCID 4/Pg 114 0 R/Type/MCR>>]/P 3624 0 R/Pg 111 0 R/S/P>>endobj3660 0 obj<</C/CM27/K 2/P 3624 0 R/Pg 114 0 R/S/P>>endobj3661 0 obj<</A 3662 0 R/K 4/P 3659 0 R/Pg 111 0 R/S/Reference>>endobj3662 0 obj<</BaselineShift 3.5/O/Layout>>endobj3663 0 obj<</A 3665 0 R/K 6/P 3655 0 R/Pg 108 0 R/S/Lbl>>endobj3664 0 obj<</K[7 3437